1:raw:FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF:0017:02:00000000
# The NEXT_HOP is 101.101.101.101 (65656565), not the 127.0.0.1 the module's
# default `self` would resolve to on this loopback session. RFC 4271 Section
# 5.1.3: "A route originated by a BGP speaker SHALL NOT be advertised to a peer
# using an address of that peer as NEXT_HOP", so ze withholds that route and
# this expectation would pin a frame ze must never send. The run script states
# --next-hop, which is the healthcheck module's own option.
1:raw:FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF:0038:02:0000001C40010100400200400304656565658004040000006440050400000064200A000001
1:raw:FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF:001C:02:0005200A0000010000
